From: OpenMANET <matthew.garcia@patriotscraft.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-overlays: morse: add RP1 (Raspberry Pi 5) MM610x SPI
 overlay

The Raspberry Pi 5 routes the 40-pin header through the RP1 southbridge,
so SPI0 and the header GPIOs live under &rp1_spi0 / &rp1_gpio instead of
the BCM283x &spi0 / &gpio nodes, and RP1 pinctrl uses the generic
pinctrl bindings (function/pins/bias-*) rather than the BCM283x
brcm,pins / brcm,function / brcm,pull properties. The existing
mm610x-spi overlay from 991-0003 therefore cannot be reused as-is.

This is added as a separate -pi5 overlay rather than as extra fragments
in mm610x-spi: the firmware overlay loader rejects an overlay outright
if any fragment target label cannot be resolved, so RP1 fragments mixed
into the shared overlay would break overlay application on Pi 3/Pi 4 and
the Seeed boards.

Wiring is identical to the Pi 4 WM1302 / Wio-WM6108 mapping in 991-0003:
  reset   GPIO17
  power   GPIO23, GPIO24
  spi-irq GPIO5
  CS      GPIO8 (CE0), driven as a GPIO chip select
  SPI0    GPIO9/10/11

SPI clock is set to 25 MHz for bring-up rather than the 50 MHz the Pi 4
overlay asks for. On BCM2835 a requested 50 MHz is actually rounded down
to 41.67 MHz (250 MHz core clock, even divisors only), so 50 MHz has
never really been exercised on this hardware. RP1's DW-SSI is fed from
clk_sys at 200 MHz, also even-divisors-only, so 50 MHz would be a true
50 MHz - 20 percent faster than the Pi 4 has ever run - and there are
field reports of MM6108-on-RP1 links being unstable at that rate.
200/8 = 25 MHz is exact. Raise this to 33.3 or 50 MHz once a two-node
link has been validated on real hardware.

Two deliberate differences from the naive RP1 translation:

  * spidev@0 / spidev@1 are explicitly disabled. bcm2712-rpi.dtsi
    declares both spidev nodes under &spi0 (== &rp1_spi0) with no
    status property, so they are enabled as soon as the controller is,
    and spidev@0 would claim CE0 alongside the MM6108.

  * chip select uses a dedicated rp1_morse_cs group that muxes GPIO8 to
    function "gpio" instead of reusing rp1_spi0_cs_gpio7, which muxes
    GPIO7+GPIO8 to the hardware "spi0" chip-select function. The Morse
    driver drives CS as a GPIO descriptor (cs-gpios, see 991-0007), and
    this mirrors what 991-0003 does on BCM283x, where spi0_cs_pins is
    overridden to BCM2835_FSEL_GPIO_OUT for the same reason.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/mm610x-spi-pi5-overlay.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@
+/dts-v1/;
+/plugin/;
+
+/ {
+	compatible = "brcm,bcm2712";
+
+	fragment@0 {
+		target = <&rp1_spi0>;
+		frag0: __overlay__ {
+			pinctrl-names = "default";
+			pinctrl-0 = <&rp1_spi0_gpio9 &rp1_morse_cs
+			             &rp1_morse_wake &rp1_morse_busy
+			             &rp1_morse_irq &rp1_morse_reset>;
+			cs-gpios = <&rp1_gpio 8 1>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "okay";
+
+			mm6108: mm6108@0 {
+				compatible = "morse,mm610x-spi";
+				reg = <0>; /* CE0 */
+				reset-gpios = <&rp1_gpio 17 0>;
+				power-gpios = <&rp1_gpio 23 0>,
+				              <&rp1_gpio 24 0>;
+				spi-irq-gpios = <&rp1_gpio 5 0>;
+				spi-max-frequency = <25000000>;
+				status = "okay";
+			};
+
+			spidev0: spidev@0 {
+				reg = <0>; /* CE0 */
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
+
+			spidev1: spidev@1 {
+				reg = <1>; /* CE1 */
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
+	fragment@1 {
+		target = <&rp1_gpio>;
+		__overlay__ {
+			rp1_morse_cs: rp1_morse_cs {
+				pin_cs {
+					function = "gpio";
+					pins = "gpio8";
+					bias-pull-up;
+				};
+			};
+
+			rp1_morse_wake: rp1_morse_wake {
+				pin_wake {
+					function = "gpio";
+					pins = "gpio23";
+					bias-pull-up;
+				};
+			};
+
+			rp1_morse_busy: rp1_morse_busy {
+				pin_busy {
+					function = "gpio";
+					pins = "gpio24";
+					bias-pull-down;
+				};
+			};
+
+			rp1_morse_irq: rp1_morse_irq {
+				pin_irq {
+					function = "gpio";
+					pins = "gpio5";
+					bias-pull-up;
+				};
+			};
+
+			rp1_morse_reset: rp1_morse_reset {
+				pin_reset {
+					function = "gpio";
+					pins = "gpio17";
+					bias-pull-up;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
